# Citation metadata, in the Citation File Format GitHub renders as
# "Cite this repository". `scripts/buildcitation.py` turns it into the BibTeX
# and APA shown on the site, so the two cannot disagree (R108).
#
# No `license` field yet: the licence is an owner decision still pending, and
# Zenodo will not mint a DOI without one. `doi` is added when it exists — a
# placeholder that looks like a DOI is worse than none.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or refer to this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Pashupatastra: policy-bounded autonomous security operations"
abstract: >-
  An AI-native security operations platform that correlates fragmented security
  telemetry into one intrusion, maps each step to a MITRE ATT&CK technique, and
  proposes remediation that a deterministic policy engine — not the model —
  decides whether a human must authorise. Every claim the assistant makes is
  cited against stored records and verified rather than trusted; every action
  declares its rollback and expected post-state before it runs.
authors:
  - family-names: Raval
    given-names: Preet
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-12
url: "https://pashupatastra.vercel.app"
repository-code: "https://github.com/preetraval45/PASHUPATASTRA"
keywords:
  - security operations
  - incident response
  - alert correlation
  - MITRE ATT&CK
  - bounded autonomy
  - LLM grounding
  - policy engine
